# Ralph fix_plan — iteration log + completion signal

Each iteration appends here. Future iterations read this file cold to recover context.

## Format per entry

```
## iter N · <UTC timestamp>
What I did:
- ...

What I learned:
- ...

> BLOCKER: (optional) describe anything the next iteration must resolve before continuing.

Next:
- one-line hint for iter N+1
```

## Completion signal

When **every** completion criterion in `PROMPT.md` is met, append a line consisting of the literal opening tag `<` then `promise` then `>COMPLETE<` then `/promise>` (i.e. the same tag used in PROMPT.md). The harness greps for that exact 31-byte string in this file and exits the loop.

(This template intentionally does NOT contain the literal marker — otherwise the harness would think you're already done before iter 1.)

